Compiling 3.7.1 is quite a headache
a few problems I came across that are bound to come up again:

- weird errors in compilation, something about PIC:
  I think this was a bug in upstream, there a patch to the Makefile that fixes this:

all: vmlinux

+KBUILD_CFLAGS += $(call cc-option, -fno-pie)
+KBUILD_CFLAGS += $(call cc-option, -no-pie)
+KBUILD_AFLAGS += $(call cc-option, -fno-pie)
+KBUILD_CPPFLAGS += $(call cc-option, -fno-pie)

insert these 4 lines that add flags in the main Makefile after all: vmlinux (around line ~500)

- Weird errors in perl scripts, probably because of new versions,
need to manually edit the perl script in `kernel/timeconst.pl`, line 373:

```
- if (!defined(@val)) {
+ if (!(@val)) {
```

(I guess "defined" is no longer supported.)

- Make sure to compile for the correct architecture, by using "ARCH=" (probably i386)

- gcc versions, should compile kernel with gcc-4.9, add a parameter in the compilation command:
`make ARCH=i386 CC="gcc-4.9" -j8 bzImage`, of course gcc-4.9 needs to be installed.
